  "title": "Tektronix 11401 Digitizing Oscilloscope",
  "year": "1986",
  "subtitle": "The laboratory oscilloscope whose front panel became a touchscreen menu system — few knobs, the panel surface itself is software",
  "why_scout_cares": "The Tektronix 11401/11402/11403 (1986-1989) is the museum's first touchscreen laboratory instrument and its clearest case of an instrument's front panel becoming a graphical interface. The 11K series replaced the knob-and-button 7K scopes with 'a touch screen and menu system' and 'few controls on the mainframe or plug-ins.' This is a direct-manipulation instrument — the machine's entire operating surface collapsed into a touchscreen GUI, a decade before touchscreens reached everyday devices. It pairs with the museum's Tektronix 7854 (a knob-and-soft-key computer scope) as the two poles of reconfigurable-instrument HCI.",
